{"name":"Explorer Khaki","hex":"#b6ac95","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"explorer","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One who explores something","A person who by means of travel (notably an expedition) searches out new information."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/explorer"},{"term":"khaki","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A dull, yellowish-brown colour, the colour of dust.","Khaki green, a dull green colour."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Dust-coloured; of the colour of dust."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/khaki"}],"entries":[{"title":"Exploration","blocks":[{"text":"Exploration is the process of exploring, an activity which has some expectation of discovery. Organised exploration is largely a human activity, but exploratory activity is common to most organisms capable of directed locomotion and the ability to learn, and has been described in, amongst others, social insects foraging behaviour, where feedback from returning individuals affects the activity of other members of the group."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Exploration"},{"title":"Khaki","blocks":[{"text":"The color khaki is a light shade of tan with a slight yellowish tinge."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Marineoffiziere_in_Dakar_%281994%29.jpg/330px-Marineoffiziere_in_Dakar_%281994%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Khaki"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Theatrum_Orbis_Terrarum%2C_by_Abraham_Ortelius%2C_World%2C_1572.jpg/500px-Theatrum_Orbis_Terrarum%2C_by_Abraham_Ortelius%2C_World%2C_1572.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Theatrum_Orbis_Terrarum%2C_by_Abraham_Ortelius%2C_World%2C_1572.jpg/1280px-Theatrum_Orbis_Terrarum%2C_by_Abraham_Orteli